shows every change below. The example/ app was not imported.

Why a copy
----------
The exam app shows question content and Desmos in exactly two WebView2
"islands" drawn into Flutter textures (architecture §2.4–2.6). The islands
must behave like part of a native app and must never become a browser, so
the lockdown is enforced in native code, before the first navigation,
instead of trusting Dart callers to configure it.

Patches (all marked "MasterSAT patch" in the source)
-----------------------------------------------------
Identity
  1. Package renamed to ms_webview2, plugin class MsWebview2Plugin, CMake
     target ms_webview2_plugin, method/event channels
     `mastersat/ms_webview2[/<id>[/events]]` (was io.jns.webview.win), so it
     can never collide with an upstream copy. migration_guide.md and the
     webview_windows.dart alias removed.

Settings applied to every webview at creation (windows/webview.cc,
ApplyIslandSettings)
  2. AreBrowserAcceleratorKeysEnabled = FALSE (F5, Ctrl+R, Ctrl+F, Ctrl+P,
     F12, Alt+Left, Ctrl+wheel... do nothing).
  3. AreDefaultContextMenusEnabled = FALSE (upstream default kept, now
     enforced here too).
  4. AreDevToolsEnabled = FALSE unless MS_WEBVIEW2_DEVTOOLS is defined
     (Debug and test builds only); setDevToolsEnabled(true) and
     openDevTools() fail in release builds.
  5. IsStatusBarEnabled, IsZoomControlEnabled, IsPinchZoomEnabled,
     IsSwipeNavigationEnabled, IsGeneralAutofillEnabled,
     IsPasswordAutosaveEnabled, AreHostObjectsAllowed,
     IsBuiltInErrorPageEnabled, AreDefaultScriptDialogsEnabled = FALSE.
  6. ZoomFactor fixed at 1.0 (app zoom is a CSS variable inside the island,
     so 1 CSS px = 1 Flutter logical px); DefaultBackgroundColor white.
  6a. SetVirtualHostNameToFolderMapping("island.mastersat.example",
     <exe dir>\data\island, DENY_CORS) at creation (MapIslandFolder), so the
     island pages resolve before Dart does anything; Dart may still re-map.

Island policy (windows/ms_policy.{h,cc}, unit-tested in
windows/test/ms_policy_test.cc)
  7. NavigationStarting cancels every top-level navigation that does not
     start with https://island.mastersat.example/ ; FrameNavigationStarting
     additionally allows about:blank / about:srcdoc.
  8. NewWindowRequested is always Handled with no window (denied), whatever
     setPopupWindowPolicy says.
  9. WebResourceRequested (filter "*") answers 403 to anything that is not
     the island host over https, blob:, data: or about:, or an https host the
     app allowed for that island with the new setAllowedResourceHosts()
     (the Desmos island allows www.desmos.com and *.desmos.com).
 10. DownloadStarting is cancelled; PermissionRequested is denied natively
     (the Dart permissionRequested delegate is never consulted any more);
     LaunchingExternalUriScheme is cancelled; script dialogs are swallowed.
     Each refusal is reported to Dart as a `blocked` event (onBlocked).

Environment (windows/webview_host.cc, webview_platform.cc,
ms_webview2_plugin.cc)
 11. Default user data folder %LOCALAPPDATA%\MasterSAT\wv2 (was
     %LOCALAPPDATA%\flutter_webview_windows\<exe>), one environment shared
     by both islands, outside the Velopack install folder.
 12. Release builds remove WEBVIEW2_ADDITIONAL_BROWSER_ARGUMENTS,
     WEBVIEW2_BROWSER_EXECUTABLE_FOLDER, WEBVIEW2_USER_DATA_FOLDER,
     WEBVIEW2_RELEASE_CHANNEL_PREFERENCE, WEBVIEW2_CHANNEL_SEARCH_KIND,
     WEBVIEW2_PIPE_FOR_SCRIPT_DEBUGGER and WEBVIEW2_WAIT_FOR_SCRIPT_DEBUGGER
     from the process environment before creating the environment, so a
     student cannot attach a debugger or swap the browser. Test builds
     (MS_WEBVIEW2_TEST_BUILD, CMake option or env var at configure time)
     honour and merge WEBVIEW2_ADDITIONAL_BROWSER_ARGUMENTS (Playwright over
     --remote-debugging-port, architecture §9 tier D).
 13. Fluent overlay scroll bars (ScrollBarStyle = FLUENT_OVERLAY).
 14. ProcessFailed is forwarded to Dart (onProcessFailed, with kind, reason
     and exit code). When the browser process exits, the plugin marks the
     shared environment dead and the next webview is created on a fresh
     one; old environments are kept alive until no webview uses them.

New Dart API (lib/src/webview.dart)
 15. WebviewController.capturePreview() -> PNG bytes (WebView2
     CapturePreview), used for windowed-mode freeze-frames and screenshots.
 16. WebviewController.setVisible(bool): IsVisible + MemoryUsageTargetLevel
     LOW while hidden / NORMAL when shown, and the texture stops producing
     frames while hidden (a resize while hidden does not restart it).
 17. WebviewController.setAllowedResourceHosts(List<String>) (see 9).
 18. WebviewController.webMessageRaw: the undecoded JSON text of each web
     message, so the app validates exactly what the page sent.
 19. Webview(cursorMapper: ...) maps the cursor WebView2 asks for before it
     is shown (the app maps the hand cursor to the arrow: no hand cursor).
 20. WebviewProcessFailedKind, WebviewProcessFailure, WebviewBlockedEvent.
 20a. Webview::RequestRepaint (windows/webview.cc): whenever the texture
     capture (re)starts — the first setSize, setVisible(true), resume — the
     webview is hidden and shown again so it presents a fresh frame.
     Windows.Graphics.Capture only delivers changes made after StartCapture,
     so a page painted before the capture began stayed blank until it changed.

Tests
 21. test/ms_patches_test.dart covers the Dart half of 15–20; upstream's
     test file is kept (renamed ms_webview2_test.dart, channel names
     updated). windows/test gained ms_policy_test.cc.

Unchanged
  The texture bridge (Windows.Graphics.Capture -> D3D11 shared handle ->
  Flutter GpuSurfaceTexture), pointer/keyboard forwarding, focus
  coordination and every other upstream behaviour.
